tion/worked-solution "From the diagram, we see that\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{OQ}=\\overset{\\to }{OL}+\\overset{\\to }{LQ}.\n$$\n\nWe're told that $\\overset{\\to }{OL}=l,$ so we just need to work out $\\overset{\\to }{LQ}.$\n\nFirst, from $△OLP,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{LP} & =\\overset{\\to }{LO}+\\overset{\\to }{OP} \\\\  & =-\\overset{\\to }{OL}+\\overset{\\to }{OP} \\\\  & =-l+p \\\\  & =p-l.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $LQ:QP=7:9,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{LQ}=\\frac{7}{16}\\overset{\\to }{LP}=\\frac{7}{16}(p-l).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{OQ} & =\\overset{\\to }{OL}+\\overset{\\to }{LQ} \\\\  & =l+\\frac{7}{16}(p-l) \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{16}l+\\frac{7}{16}p.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-322586/field-1" "q-322586/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "feae36e7-ae88-5f3a-957f-e65a92e399ad"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-322586"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-120294/selection/7d678816a8ca1ec614595685c9a9bfc86b4f0011d2fb82903d42a3662ffdb374" :answer/id #uuid "119bbc1f-77cb-5f6e-841f-a7461d0af059" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\overset{\\to }{OW}=\\frac{5}{7}u+\\frac{2}{7}v" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-120294/selection/82139e72a4689c2ef5e4364ec70af216b0fd3e660aa73d71a678e6a1009e5e9d" :answer/id #uuid "eff802b1-731c-51b7-bf9a-9e37d4effaf6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\overset{\\to }{OW}=\\frac{7}{9}u+\\frac{2}{9}v" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-120294/selection/58605b59f5021b3005c3136e1d9f6fbf602d30a3ad99f11d5490f00670f7b539" :answer/id #uuid "2b26e8dc-381e-5cd8-bd1f-6e5ce6c2a927" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\overset{\\to }{OW}=\\frac{1}{3}u+\\frac{2}{3}v" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-120294/selection/675350ba512a57a76d6261104f69ca401f339b3f471f2185b9554d7056963245" :answer/id #uuid "4520e6dd-1096-51b7-902f-810bba3287fc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\overset{\\to }{OW}=\\frac{2}{9}u+\\frac{7}{9}v" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-120294/selection/c2573f9111683d84898e586b757b5e1741e02681e5f7f2b404c0ee79bf6568a4" :answer/id #uuid "645d11af-3b90-5cd4-bcae-747f6464c24d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\overset{\\to }{OW}=\\frac{2}{3}u+\\frac{1}{3}v" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-120294/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "44fd3dc6-4a28-5719-899d-335c26b0b275" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-120294/selection/675350ba512a57a76d6261104f69ca401f339b3f471f2185b9554d7056963245" :answer-field/choices ["q-120294/selection/7d678816a8ca1ec614595685c9a9bfc86b4f0011d2fb82903d42a3662ffdb374" "q-120294/selection/82139e72a4689c2ef5e4364ec70af216b0fd3e660aa73d71a678e6a1009e5e9d" "q-120294/selection/58605b59f5021b3005c3136e1d9f6fbf602d30a3ad99f11d5490f00670f7b539" "q-120294/selection/675350ba512a57a76d6261104f69ca401f339b3f471f2185b9554d7056963245" "q-120294/selection/c2573f9111683d84898e586b757b5e1741e02681e5f7f2b404c0ee79bf6568a4"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-120294" :question/id #uuid "426f1843-d9cb-5293-a83b-9e7101ceab9e" :question/math-academy-id "q-120294" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073957/assets/707beca1d856414e25874cc0b56c6654fbb41d699f01106b6749d49408b39aee.png)\n\nConsider the diagram above, where $\\overset{\\to }{OU}=u,$ $\\overset{\\to }{OV}=v$ and $W$ divides $\\overset{―}{UV}$ in the ratio $UW:WV=7:2.$ Find $\\overset{\\to }{OW}.$" :question/worked-solution "From the diagram, we see that\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{OW}=\\overset{\\to }{OU}+\\overset{\\to }{UW}.\n$$\n\nWe're told that $\\overset{\\to }{OU}=u,$ so we just need to work out $\\overset{\\to }{UW}.$\n\nFirst, from $△OUV,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{UV} & =\\overset{\\to }{UO}+\\overset{\\to }{OV} \\\\  & =-\\overset{\\to }{OU}+\\overset{\\to }{OV} \\\\  & =-u+v \\\\  & =v-u.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $UW:WV=7:2,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{UW}=\\frac{7}{9}\\overset{\\to }{UV}=\\frac{7}{9}(v-u).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{OW} & =\\overset{\\to }{OU}+\\overset{\\to }{UW} \\\\  & =u+\\frac{7}{9}(v-u) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{9}u+\\frac{7}{9}v.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-120294/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "feae36e7-ae88-5f3a-957f-e65a92e399ad"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-120294"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-278263/field-1/8de7a84a41666d4612460439d17949f75cc9ba4883ff75d5034a1786c2a06792" :answer/id #uuid "62a91400-1394-5c71-bf24-68c563c8b75a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-278263/field-1/8bb646af439794acfbd313a6a7eb86a2818f1f792118f7583677724bca2d9903" :answer/id #uuid "9891f941-47e3-5915-8ca6-8f696a84c886" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-278263/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "a1579070-7bd6-5ee9-b6a5-af394ba37133" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-278263/field-1/8de7a84a41666d4612460439d17949f75cc9ba4883ff75d5034a1786c2a06792" :answer-field/choices ["q-278263/field-1/8de7a84a41666d4612460439d17949f75cc9ba4883ff75d5034a1786c2a06792" "q-278263/field-1/8bb646af439794acfbd313a6a7eb86a2818f1f792118f7583677724bca2d9903"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-278263/field-2/8bb646af439794acfbd313a6a7eb86a2818f1f792118f7583677724bca2d9903" :answer/id #uuid "3b3da92b-7081-5cf5-9dd9-6a96c9149ea4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-278263/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "c945b93c-4002-5736-9f1a-0e431bb90f15" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-278263/field-2/8bb646af439794acfbd313a6a7eb86a2818f1f792118f7583677724bca2d9903" :answer-field/choices ["q-278263/field-2/8bb646af439794acfbd313a6a7eb86a2818f1f792118f7583677724bca2d9903"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-278263" :question/id #uuid "3088d475-ce58-52b9-ba8a-49f9f22bb4ca" :question/math-academy-id "q-278263" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073957/assets/c26ec7e1fccc5ada4c43eef55faf9e4fa3e17ed896b1546f472edf744404da1a.png)\n\nConsider the diagram above, where $\\overset{\\to }{OD}=d,$ $\\overset{\\to }{OE}=e,$ and $F$ divides $\\overset{―}{DE}$ in the ratio $DF:FE=2:3.$ Express $\\overset{\\to }{OF}$ via the vectors $d$ and $e.$\n\n$\\,\\overset{\\to }{OF}=$\n{{field-1}}\n$d+$\n{{field-2}}\n$e$" :question/worked-solution "From the diagram, we see that\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{OF}=\\overset{\\to }{OD}+\\overset{\\to }{DF}.\n$$\n\nWe're told that $\\overset{\\to }{OD}=d,$ so we just need to work out $\\overset{\\to }{DF}.$\n\nFirst, from $△ODE,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{DE} & =\\overset{\\to }{DO}+\\overset{\\to }{OE} \\\\  & =-\\overset{\\to }{OD}+\\overset{\\to }{OE} \\\\  & =-d+e \\\\  & =e-d.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $DF:FE=2:3,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{DF}=\\frac{2}{5}\\overset{\\to }{DE}=\\frac{2}{5}(e-d).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{OF} & =\\overset{\\to }{OD}+\\overset{\\to }{DF} \\\\  & =d+\\frac{2}{5}(e-d) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{5}d+\\frac{2}{5}e.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-278263/field-1" "q-278263/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "feae36e7-ae88-5f3a-957f-e65a92e399ad"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-278263"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-322575/field-1/822babba0c51e013fbe25d1f58a63f0c96c679e636bfebc614d67d25b09a09e9" :answer/id #uuid "92dd2734-6dae-57ff-9b06-71ab3dfc49b4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{9}{13}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-322575/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "6f009688-4ef9-5753-ba65-afdb8e806572" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-322575/field-1/822babba0c51e013fbe25d1f58a63f0c96c679e636bfebc614d67d25b09a09e9" :answer-field/choices ["q-322575/field-1/822babba0c51e013fbe25d1f58a63f0c96c679e636bfebc614d67d25b09a09e9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-322575/field-2/be8a132e5ec36f879a54ab3624495e1da1ac7ce2b0a299371685f8a5e655be69" :answer/id #uuid "16ae27f2-85cc-5f94-abf0-7351c9beca1b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4}{13}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-322575/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "3ab7ba89-c18c-5247-9d73-1677eb687356" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-322575/field-2/be8a132e5ec36f879a54ab3624495e1da1ac7ce2b0a299371685f8a5e655be69" :answer-field/choices ["q-322575/field-2/be8a132e5ec36f879a54ab3624495e1da1ac7ce2b0a299371685f8a5e655be69"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-322575" :question/id #uuid "4379c333-620d-5f21-90a0-ba71841120f7" :question/math-academy-id "q-322575" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073957/assets/d9448f9f05666f9806975b37a73f09c492eb73139b6f9395b619f077f3a584c9.png)\n\nConsider the diagram above, where $\\overset{\\to }{OP}=p,$ $\\overset{\\to }{OQ}=q,$ and $R$ divides $\\overset{―}{PQ}$ in the ratio $PR:RQ=4:9.$ Express $\\overset{\\to }{OR}$ via the vectors $p$ and $q.$\n\n$\\,\\overset{\\to }{OR}=$\n{{field-1}}\n$p+$\n{{field-2}}\n$q$" :question/worked-solution "From the diagram, we see that\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{OR}=\\overset{\\to }{OP}+\\overset{\\to }{PR}.\n$$\n\nWe're told that $\\overset{\\to }{OP}=p,$ so we just need to work out $\\overset{\\to }{PR}.$\n\nFirst, from $△OPQ,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =\\overset{\\to }{PO}+\\overset{\\to }{OQ} \\\\  & =-\\overset{\\to }{OP}+\\overset{\\to }{OQ} \\\\  & =-p+q \\\\  & =q-p.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $PR:RQ=4:9,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{PR}=\\frac{4}{13}\\overset{\\to }{PQ}=\\frac{4}{13}(q-p).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{OR} & =\\overset{\\to }{OP}+\\overset{\\to }{PR} \\\\  & =p+\\frac{4}{13}(q-p) \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{13}p+\\frac{4}{13}q.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-322575/field-1" "q-322575/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "feae36e7-ae88-5f3a-957f-e65a92e399ad"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-322575"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-5212"] :question/problem "Consider the picture below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073957/assets/f2518c2e998e7c7f551548a4cc7283720a66428ea8fa9872494a81cc3848ba9e.png)\n\nGiven that ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073957/assets/c6714d0a6eaa5c7d354d46e8d6d60da7f3d2011df0fc75773036cf7ae510c5e3.png), find ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073957/assets/24878591902884f45f14f5c447bc326586a411a8870b205fc12825a4ab2c738a.png)" :question/worked-solution "Recall that when two known vectors are not parallel, a linear combination of them is unique. So, once we rewrite ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073957/assets/5c644b15efcf5a4274de23242a722604ead2ff800ea29ba7a650729227fefdf0.png) in terms of ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073957/assets/27f36b1d1846e12e3c50b7d4e47f5745727792d52a48e4d85b689ec36e3d25a0.png) 